		+ "reversible in review"
	SOURCE "Found on 2026-09-08 in the review of pull request 37"
		PR 37

LIMITATION TheMachineBreakdownIgnoresOptimizerBoost
	SYMPTOM "The production breakdown by machine uses base levels only, without the boost of"
		+ "optimizers and fuses: once a fuse is in play the totalLevel of the entries sums below"
		+ "production, and their productionRatio shares do not sum to 1"
	STATUS archived
	ARCHIVED_ON 2026-09-25
	SEEN_IN "packages/core-mapping/src/domain/PlanetEnergyGrid.ts::private"
		+ "productionBreakdown(production: number)"
	APPLIES_TO_PACKAGE @PACKAGE.core_mapping
	RATIONALE "It is the counterpart of counting the boost once, in the contribution of the"
		+ "optimizer, so as not to count it twice in the planet energy grid. A code comment carried"
		+ "it until the move to PlanetEnergyGrid removed it"
		REF @DECISION.APlanetEnergyGridIsAnAggregate
	SOURCE "Found on 2026-09-13 while moving the energy rules into PlanetEnergyGrid"
		PR 72

LIMITATION EachCliDuplicatesItsVersionAndUnknownArgumentRendering
	SYMPTOM "renderVersion and renderUnknownArguments are written twice, once in cli-merge and once"
		+ "in cli-validate, and fallow reports the pair as a clone group unless its reviewed key is"
		+ "listed"
	WORKAROUND "The clone group is listed as reviewed under its exact key in fallow.toml, which"
		+ "lapses as soon as either copy changes or a third copy appears; a change to one copy is"
		+ "made to the other"
	UNTIL "a package the dependency matrix lets both cli-* packages import can hold terminal"
		+ "rendering, or a third CLI needs the same lines"
	SEEN_IN "packages/cli-merge/cli/renderMergeCliOutput.js::renderVersion"
	SEEN_IN "packages/cli-validate/cli/renderValidateCliOutput.js::renderVersion"
	SEEN_IN "fallow.toml::ignoredClones"
	APPLIES_TO_PACKAGE @PACKAGE.cli_merge
	APPLIES_TO_PACKAGE @PACKAGE.cli_validate
	RATIONALE "No shared home is allowed today: a shared-* package holds no UI concern (ARCH-SHR-2)"
		+ "and terminal output is the presentation of a CLI, and a cli-* package may depend only on"
		+ "shared-*, util-* and core-* packages, so neither CLI can import the other's rendering."
		+ "Ignoring the rendering files for duplication was rejected: every later clone there would"
		+ "go unseen, where the reviewed key lapses on its own"
		REF @DECISION.BothCliEntryFilesRunThroughOneSharedFunction
	SOURCE "Pull request review, the owner asking for the fallow warnings to be resolved, then for"
		+ "the kept duplication to be recorded as a limitation rather than a decision"
		PR 135

LIMITATION TheFallowAuditReadsNoFileOfUiSaveManager
	SYMPTOM "fallow audit and fallow health skip every file of ui-save-manager: an unused export,"
		+ "an unused file, a duplicate or a complex function of the web UI fails no quality gate"
	WORKAROUND "run fallow by hand on a copy of fallow.toml without the ui-save-manager ignore"
		+ "pattern and with src/app.tsx and src/routes/*.tsx as entries"
	UNTIL @TASK.CHORE112
	SEEN_IN "fallow.toml::packages/ui-save-manager/**"
	APPLIES_TO_PACKAGE @PACKAGE.ui_save_manager
	RATIONALE "The exclusion was written at the migration as a decision with no reasoning, and"
		+ "nothing in fallow prevents the audit. Measured on 2026-09-24 with the workaround:"
		+ "dead-code reports no issue and health one high-complexity function, in"
		+ "src/routes/index.tsx"
	SOURCE "Exclusion written in the migration"
		PR 61
	SOURCE "Rewritten from a decision by the review of CHORE109"
		PR 145

LIMITATION AVersionTagCreatesNoGitHubRelease
	SYMPTOM "A pushed <tool>-v<version> tag creates no GitHub release: the Releases page of the"
		+ "repository stays empty and a watcher of releases is never notified"
	WORKAROUND "The CHANGELOG.md of each tool is its release note"
	UNTIL "a tool is distributed as a file to download, or people outside the project ask to follow"
		+ "its releases"
	SEEN_IN ".github/workflows/release.yml::contents: read"
	SEEN_IN "scripts/release/release-tag.ts::RELEASE_BRANCH"
	RATIONALE "Nothing is downloaded today: the web UI is published by hand on Netlify and both"
		+ "CLIs run from a clone. One release sets one tag per tool, so it would open up to three"
		+ "GitHub releases carrying the changelog entries again, and the Latest mark would single"
		+ "out one tool arbitrarily. Creating the release in the Release workflow after its verify"
		+ "job is the intended fix, at the cost of granting that workflow contents: write"
	SOURCE "Asked by the owner after the first release, 0.1.0, and kept as a limitation so the"
		+ "question can be reopened when the need appears"
		PR 165

LIMITATION SubmergedMachinesAreCountedAsDrawingPower
	SYMPTOM "a machine placed under water draws no power in game, but the displayed consumption"
		+ "counts it at its base level, so the available energy is underestimated"
	WORKAROUND "a warning in the energy section that submerged machines may distort the computed"
		+ "available energy"
		REF @TASK.FEAT128
	UNTIL "the save records whether a machine is under water or running"
	SEEN_IN "packages/core-mapping/src/domain/PlanetEnergyGrid.ts::private consumption()"
	APPLIES_TO_PACKAGE @PACKAGE.core_mapping
	RATIONALE "The save stores the position of a machine but neither the water level nor whether"
		+ "the machine runs. The water level differs from lake to lake and rises with the"
		+ "terraformation, so no rule on the height tells a submerged machine from one on dry"
		+ "ground: on Prime, machines standing 14 to 20 meters high on dry ground draw their full"
		+ "level while the submerged drills stand at 13"
	SOURCE "Owner's reading in game on 2026-09-25 of the private save Custom-2-max-data: on Prime"
		+ "the HUD prints a consumption of 19146.3 kW where the tool computes 19311.8 kW, and the"
		+ "165.5 kW gap is exactly one OreExtractor2 and three Drill0 placed under a lake, which"
		+ "the owner found submerged; the production matched to the kilowatt"
		PR 178
		REF @GAME_RELEASE.2.103
		REF @PROJECT.DNC
